{
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "description": "peer-advert conformance vectors for protocol version 1, the one file here built on real Ed25519 key material rather than structural filler. Beyond the usual wire_hex round trip, each vector records signing_input_hex (spec/transport.cddl's domain-separation context followed by the canonical CDE encoding of the advert with its signature entry removed) and the verdict `verifies` a conformant verifier must reach, applying both the self-certification check and the signature check. An implementation that reconstructs the signing input even one byte differently will reject every advert another implementation sends while still passing its own tests, which is exactly what freezing these bytes catches. The key is derived from a fixed seed and the algorithm is Ed25519 specifically because its signatures are deterministic (RFC 8032), so regenerating this file reproduces it byte for byte.",
